RISC OS: the window scale on high resolution (EX0 EY0) desktops.

On an EX0 EY0 ("180 dpi") desktop one OS unit is one pixel, so the game's
window came out half as wide and high as in a normal mode (and full screen
drew four times the pixels). riscos-mesa 20.3.5-16 has a window scale:
each of the program's pixels is shown as scale x scale screen pixels.
- After eglInitialize, scale = eglWindowScaleRISCOS(dpy, w, h) for the
  window's size: 2 in an EX0 EY0 mode when a window twice the size fits,
  else 1 (EGL$WindowScale 1-4 overrides it).
- The window opens (w * scale) << eig OS units; the surface gets
  EGL_WINDOW_SCALE_RISCOS = scale, so it still renders w x h.
- Every size and position the program sees (window size and position,
  mouse, FsSetMousePosition, maximise, full screen) is in its own pixels:
  screen pixels / scale.
- Message_ModeChange: the scale is worked out again for the window's size
  and set at once with eglSurfaceAttrib.
YSFlight$Render (a fixed drawing size) still takes precedence in EGL.
Host test: tests/host-window (scale 2 checks).

